      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "L4 and L7",
      "items": [
        "L4 routes TCP or UDP connections from transport metadata; TLS may pass through or terminate depending on the product",
        "L7 understands HTTP semantics and can route HTTP, HTTPS, or gRPC by host, path, header, or other request data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Algorithms distribute work, not CPU",
      "items": [
        "Round robin, weights, least connections, or hashing select a target according to product capabilities",
        "Long-lived connections, affinity, and unequal request cost can still produce uneven utilization"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Two health decisions",
      "items": [
        "Traffic readiness controls new routing after success or failure thresholds",
        "Instance health can trigger replacement; it does not mean demand increased, and draining protects in-flight work"
